# The backend image's build context is the repo root (see modules/backend/
# Dockerfile's COPY list: config.yaml, modules/backend, lib/, scripts/).
#
# data/ is none of that — it is the appliance's live state: intact.db, the fused
# graph sidecars, and the upgrade engine's temp dirs. On a box that has run an
# upgrade it is over a gigabyte, some of it root-owned, so `docker build` on the
# appliance failed outright ("error from sender: permission denied") and every
# successful build before that had been shipping the live case database to the
# docker daemon for no reason.
data/

# Never ship local operator state or build spoil into a context either.
*.upgrade-bak-*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The rest of a live box's untracked bulk and secrets. None of it is under the
# Dockerfile's COPY list, but `docker build` still sends the whole context to
# the daemon, so on a box that meant the GitHub token in
# config.yaml.pre-upgrade-backup, every module's secrets/ and certs, and the
# Velociraptor client binaries. Patterns match from the context root, so `*.log`
# alone would only catch top-level logs.
.git/
.pytest_cache/
**/*.log
config.yaml.*
backups/
client_installers/
**/secrets
modules/*/.env
modules/nginx/ssl/
modules/nginx/html/downloads/
modules/velociraptor/clients/
modules/iris/config/certificates/
modules/timesketch/config/timesketch*.conf
